{#-
  Compare the production integration against the read-only shadow copy,
  entity by entity. Paste into Developer Tools -> Template; it needs no token
  and no files on the Home Assistant box.

  What it is for: production reads the heat pump through hand-rolled pymodbus
  calls, the shadow through Home Assistant's shared connection on the tmodbus
  backend. The two share no transport code at all. If a register block were
  planned differently, or a signed value decoded differently, the result would
  still look like a plausible temperature -- it would land in the statistics
  looking like data. Reading both at once and diffing them is what makes that
  failure loud.

  The comparison walks the SHADOW entities and looks up the production twin,
  not the other way round: production also carries template and statistics
  sensors that were never part of the integration (thermal_power_*,
  compressor_speed_*_58min), and those have no counterpart by design.

  Reading the output: the two sides poll at different intervals (10 s against
  300 s), so the shadow's numbers lag by up to five minutes. Anything that
  moves quickly -- hot gas temperature during a compressor start, flow rate at
  pump switch-on, the compressor and defrost flags -- can differ honestly.
  Anything that moves slowly must agree, and everything must agree while the
  machine is idle. The age of both samples is printed so a delta can be judged
  against how stale the reading is.

  A binary sensor that differs while the compressor is running is noise. A
  temperature off by a whole degree at standby, a pressure off by any amount,
  or the same row differing across several runs is not.

  Rows are collected into a list and joined at the end. Emitting them inside
  the loop looks simpler but loses the line breaks to whitespace control.
-#}
{%- set shadow_prefix = 'thermav_testkopie_' -%}
{%- set prod_prefix = 'lg_thermav_r290_' -%}

{#- Absolute tolerance by entity-id suffix. Everything unlisted must match
    exactly: register contents that are codes, not measurements. -#}
{%- set tolerances = [
  ('_hot_gas_temperature',           8.0),
  ('_suction_temperature',           4.0),
  ('_temperature_before_evaporator', 4.0),
  ('_temperature_after_evaporator',  4.0),
  ('_liquid_gas_temperature',        4.0),
  ('_high_pressure_condenser',       4.0),
  ('_low_pressure_evaporator',       4.0),
  ('_flow_rate',                     6.0),
  ('_compressor_speed',            300.0),
  ('_outlet_temperature',            2.0),
  ('_inlet_temperature',             2.0),
  ('_backup_heater_outlet_temperature', 2.0),
  ('_dhw_temperature',               1.0),
  ('_flow_temperature_circuit_2',    1.0),
  ('_water_pressure',                0.3),
  ('_outdoor_temperature',           0.5),
  ('_solar_collector_temperature',   0.5),
  ('_room_air_temperature_circuit_1', 0.5),
  ('_room_air_temperature_circuit_2', 0.5),
  ('_operation_cycle_odu',           1.0)
] -%}

{%- set tolerance_of = dict(tolerances) -%}
{%- set ns = namespace(rows=[], diff=[], missing=[], ok=0, total=0) -%}
{%- for domain in ['sensor', 'binary_sensor'] -%}
  {%- for e in states[domain] if shadow_prefix in e.entity_id -%}
    {%- set key = e.entity_id.split(shadow_prefix)[1] -%}
    {%- set prod_id = domain ~ '.' ~ prod_prefix ~ key -%}
    {%- set ns.total = ns.total + 1 -%}
    {%- if not has_value(prod_id) -%}
      {%- set ns.missing = ns.missing + [key] -%}
      {%- set ns.rows = ns.rows + ['%-38s %-14s %-14s %-9s %s' | format(
           key, states(prod_id), e.state, '-', 'KEIN PARTNER')] -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- set p = states(prod_id) -%}
      {%- set t = e.state -%}
      {%- set numeric = p is match('^-?[0-9.]+$') and t is match('^-?[0-9.]+$') -%}
      {%- set limit = tolerance_of.get('_' ~ key, 0.0) -%}
      {%- if numeric -%}
        {%- set d = p | float - t | float -%}
        {%- set good = (d | abs) <= limit -%}
        {%- set delta = d | round(2) -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- set good = p == t -%}
        {%- set delta = '=' if good else '!=' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if good -%}{%- set ns.ok = ns.ok + 1 -%}
      {%- else -%}{%- set ns.diff = ns.diff + [key] -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- set ns.rows = ns.rows + ['%-38s %-14s %-14s %-9s %s' | format(
           key, p, t, delta,
           'ok' if good else ('ABWEICHUNG (Grenze ' ~ limit ~ ')' if numeric
                              else 'ABWEICHUNG'))] -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- set p_age = (now() - states.sensor.lg_thermav_r290_outlet_temperature.last_updated).total_seconds() | round(0) -%}
{%- set t_ent = states.sensor.thermav_testkopie_outlet_temperature -%}
{%- set t_age = (now() - t_ent.last_updated).total_seconds() | round(0) if t_ent else -1 -%}
{%- set running = is_state('binary_sensor.lg_thermav_r290_compressor', 'on') -%}
{%- if ns.total == 0 -%}
Keine Entitaeten mit dem Praefix "{{ shadow_prefix }}" gefunden.
Ist der Config-Entry "LG ThermaV R290 (Testkopie, nur lesend)" schon angelegt?
{%- else -%}
{{ '%-38s %-14s %-14s %-9s %s' | format('Groesse', 'produktiv', 'Testkopie', 'Delta', 'Status') }}
{{ '-' * 95 }}
{{ ns.rows | join('\n') }}
{{ '-' * 95 }}
{{ ns.ok }} von {{ ns.total }} innerhalb der Toleranz.
{% if ns.diff %}Auffaellig: {{ ns.diff | join(', ') }}
{% endif %}{% if ns.missing %}Ohne Partner: {{ ns.missing | join(', ') }}
{% endif %}Alter der Stichproben: produktiv {{ p_age }} s, Testkopie {{ t_age }} s
Zeitpunkt: {{ now().strftime('%d.%m.%Y %H:%M:%S') }}
Verdichter: {{ 'LAEUFT' if running else 'steht' }} -- {{
  'Schnelle Groessen duerfen jetzt abweichen, langsame nicht.' if running
  else 'Im Stillstand muss praktisch alles zusammenfallen; jede Abweichung ist ein Befund.' }}
{%- endif -%}
